<?php

namespace Sabre\VObject;

/**
 * Type information for a library that ships none.
 *
 * `Sabre\VObject\Node` implements `IteratorAggregate` and `ArrayAccess` without
 * declaring what they hold, so every parameter typed as a `VEvent` — or any
 * other component — trips PHPStan's `missingType.iterableValue`. There is
 * nothing wrong with the calling code; the analyser simply has no way to know
 * that iterating a node yields child nodes, or that `$event['SUMMARY']` is
 * addressed by string.
 *
 * A stub rather than a baseline entry or an `@phpstan-ignore`: those hide the
 * finding, this answers it.
 *
 * `Sabre\Xml\XmlSerializable` is deliberately **not** repeated here. A stub
 * replaces the class it describes, and naming an interface PHPStan resolves
 * from a different package makes the stub itself the error. Nothing in this
 * application serialises a node to XML, so the omission costs nothing — and if
 * something ever does, it will be a missing-method error rather than a silent
 * wrong answer.
 *
 * @implements \IteratorAggregate<int, Node>
 * @implements \ArrayAccess<string, Node|null>
 */
abstract class Node implements \IteratorAggregate, \ArrayAccess, \Countable, \JsonSerializable
{
}
